  "period_note": "Balance sheet is the period-end snapshot (reported), Solo basis, from First Security Islami Bank PLC's own Condensed Balance Sheet (Un-audited) as at 2024-06-30. Income-statement items with a '_cumulative' suffix are cumulative from 1 January of the same year; items with a '_discrete_q' suffix are the single discrete quarter alone -- both are printed directly as separate columns in the source document (not derived by subtraction), so both carry basis='reported'. The comparative prior-year-end Total Assets column in this filing cross-validates exactly (to the taka, after rounding) against this dataset's already-stored 659,114.06mn (2023_Q4.json) total_assets figure, confirming Solo basis continuity and no restatement between the audited annual figure and this interim filing's own comparative column. Cumulative (Jan-Jun) and discrete (Apr-Jun) columns both directly reported. Net Profit After Tax for the Apr-Jun 2024 quarter alone was BDT +528.20mn (H1 cumulative BDT +889.23mn minus Q1's BDT +361.03mn) -- still solidly profitable and in fact higher than Q1, though H1-cumulative profit of BDT 889.23mn was already down ~25% versus H1 2023's BDT 1,189.58mn. Cumulative Specific Provision for Classified Investment reached BDT +593.78mn by H1 (i.e. ~BDT 449.25mn charged in Q2 alone, ~3.1x Q1's charge, and a sharp reversal from H1 2023's net -573.50mn RELEASE) -- the acceleration in provisioning that would culminate in the FY2024 collapse was already visible, in real time, in this unaudited filing dated 2024-07-31, well before the audited FY2024 results (finalized ~2025-05-29) revealed the full scale of the crisis.",
